```rust
pub fn version_is_newer(current: &str, latest: &str) -> bool {
    let parse = |s: &str| -> Vec<u64> {
        s.split('.')
            .map(|part| {
                // Strip any SemVer pre-release (-beta.1) or build (+5) suffix so
                // the numeric core still compares correctly.
                let core = part.split(['-', '+']).next().unwrap_or(part);
                core.parse::<u64>().unwrap_or(0)
            })
            .collect()
    };
    ...
}
```

This is a small, concrete improvement: correctly handles pre-release/build-metadata tags. Add a test for it.

Note: per SemVer, `1.0.0-alpha` < `1.0.0`. My change compares the numeric core only, so `version_is_newer("0.1.17", "0.1.18-beta.1")` → true (correct — 0.1.18-beta is indeed newer than 0.1.17). And `version_is_newer("0.1.18", "0.1.18-beta.1")` → false (numeric core equal, correct-ish; SemVer says alpha < release, so false is right). Good enough and strictly better than before.

